    ('What does logging.disable() do?', "`logging.disable()`: Disable all logging calls of severity 'level' and below."),
    ('What does logging.error() do?', "`logging.error()`: Log a message with severity 'ERROR' on the root logger. If the logger has no handlers, call basicConfig() to add a console handler with a pre-defined format."),
    ('What does logging.exception() do?', "`logging.exception()`: Log a message with severity 'ERROR' on the root logger, with exception information. If the logger has no handlers, basicConfig() is called to add a console handler with a pre-defined format."),
    ('What does logging.fatal() do?', "`logging.fatal()`: Don't use this function, use critical() instead."),
    ('What does logging.getHandlerByName() do?', "`logging.getHandlerByName()`: Get a handler with the specified *name*, or None if there isn't one with that name."),
    ('What does logging.getHandlerNames() do?', '`logging.getHandlerNames()`: Return all known handler names as an immutable set.'),
    ('What does logging.getLevelName() do?', "`logging.getLevelName()`: Return the textual or numeric representation of logging level 'level'."),
    ('What does logging.getLogRecordFactory() do?', '`logging.getLogRecordFactory()`: Return the factory to be used when instantiating a log record.'),
    ('What does logging.getLogger() do?', '`logging.getLogger()`: Return a logger with the specified name, creating it if necessary.'),
    ('What does logging.getLoggerClass() do?', '`logging.getLoggerClass()`: Return the class to be used when instantiating a logger.'),
    ('What does logging.info() do?', "`logging.info()`: Log a message with severity 'INFO' on the root logger. If the logger has no handlers, call basicConfig() to add a console handler with a pre-defined format."),
    ('What does logging.log() do?', "`logging.log()`: Log 'msg % args' with the integer severity 'level' on the root logger. If the logger has no handlers, call basicConfig() to add a console handler with a pre-defined format."),
    ('What does logging.makeLogRecord() do?', '`logging.makeLogRecord()`: Make a LogRecord whose attributes are defined by the specified dictionary, This function is useful for converting a logging event received over a socket connection (which is sent as a dictionary) into a LogRecord instance.'),
    ('What does logging.setLogRecordFactory() do?', '`logging.setLogRecordFactory()`: Set the factory to be used when instantiating a log record.'),
    ('What does logging.setLoggerClass() do?', '`logging.setLoggerClass()`: Set the class to be used when instantiating a logger. The class should define __init__() such that only a name argument is required, and the __init__() should call Logger.__init__()'),
    ('What does logging.shutdown() do?', '`logging.shutdown()`: Perform any cleanup actions in the logging system (e.g. flushing buffers).'),
    ('What does logging.warning() do?', "`logging.warning()`: Log a message with severity 'WARNING' on the root logger. If the logger has no handlers, call basicConfig() to add a console handler with a pre-defined format."),
    ('What does logging.handlers.BaseRotatingHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.BaseRotatingHandler()`: Base class for handlers that rotate log files at a certain point. Not meant to be instantiated directly. Instead, use RotatingFileHandler or TimedRotatingFileHandler.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.BufferingHandler() do?', "`logging.handlers.BufferingHandler()`: A handler class which buffers logging records in memory. Whenever each record is added to the buffer, a check is made to see if the buffer should be flushed. If it should, then flush() is expected to do what's needed."),
    ('What does logging.handlers.DatagramHandler() do?', "`logging.handlers.DatagramHandler()`: A handler class which writes logging records, in pickle format, to a datagram socket. The pickle which is sent is that of the LogRecord's attribute dictionary (__dict__), so that the receiver does not need to have the logging module installed in order to process the logging event."),
    ('What does logging.handlers.HTTPHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.HTTPHandler()`: A class which sends records to a web server, using either GET or POST semantics.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.MemoryHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.MemoryHandler()`: A handler class which buffers logging records in memory, periodically flushing them to a target handler. Flushing occurs whenever the buffer is full, or when an event of a certain severity or greater is seen.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.NTEventLogHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.NTEventLogHandler()`: A handler class which sends events to the NT Event Log.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.QueueHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.QueueHandler()`: This handler sends events to a queue. Typically, it would be used together with a multiprocessing Queue to centralise logging to file in one process (in a multi-process application), so as to avoid file write contention between processes.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.QueueListener() do?', '`logging.handlers.QueueListener()`: This class implements an internal threaded listener which watches for LogRecords being added to a queue, removes them and passes them to a list of handlers for processing.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.RotatingFileHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.RotatingFileHandler()`: Handler for logging to a set of files, which switches from one file to the next when the current file reaches a certain size.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.SMTPHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.SMTPHandler()`: A handler class which sends an SMTP email for each logging event.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.SocketHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.SocketHandler()`: A handler class which writes logging records, in pickle format, to a streaming socket.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.SysLogHandler() do?', "`logging.handlers.SysLogHandler()`: A handler class which sends formatted logging records to a syslog server. Based on Sam Rushing's syslog module: http://www.nightmare.com/squirl/python-ext/misc/syslog.py Contributed by Nicolas Untz (after which minor refactoring changes have been made)."),
    ('What does logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler()`: Handler for logging to a file, rotating the log file at certain timed intervals.'),
    ('What does logging.handlers.WatchedFileHandler() do?', '`logging.handlers.WatchedFileHandler()`: A handler for logging to a file, which watches the file to see if it has changed while in use.'),
    ('What does lzma.LZMAFile() do?', '`lzma.LZMAFile()`: A file object providing transparent LZMA (de)compression.'),
    ('What does lzma.compress() do?', '`lzma.compress()`: Compress a block of data.'),
    ('What does lzma.decompress() do?', '`lzma.decompress()`: Decompress a block of data.'),
    ('What does lzma.open() do?', '`lzma.open()`: Open an LZMA-compressed file in binary or text mode.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.MimeTypes() do?', '`mimetypes.MimeTypes()`: MIME-types datastore.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.add_type() do?', '`mimetypes.add_type()`: Add a mapping between a type and an extension.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.guess_all_extensions() do?', '`mimetypes.guess_all_extensions()`: Guess the extensions for a file based on its MIME type.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.guess_extension() do?', '`mimetypes.guess_extension()`: Guess the extension for a file based on its MIME type.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.guess_file_type() do?', '`mimetypes.guess_file_type()`: Guess the type of a file based on its path.'),
    ('What does mimetypes.guess_type() do?', '`mimetypes.guess_type()`: Guess the type of a file based on its URL.'),
    ('What does mmap.mmap() do?', '`mmap.mmap()`: Windows: mmap(fileno, length[, tagname[, access[, offset]]])'),
    ('What does multiprocessing.pool.MaybeEncodingError() do?', '`multiprocessing.pool.MaybeEncodingError()`: Wraps possible unpickleable errors, so they can be safely sent through the socket.'),
    ('What does multiprocessing.pool.Pool() do?', '`multiprocessing.pool.Pool()`: Class which supports an async version of applying functions to arguments.'),
    ('What does os.PathLike() do?', '`os.PathLike()`: Abstract base class for implementing the file system path protocol.'),
    ('What does os.execl() do?', '`os.execl()`: Execute the executable file with argument list args, replacing the current process.'),
    ('What does os.execle() do?', '`os.execle()`: Execute the executable file with argument list args and environment env, replacing the current process.'),
    ('What does os.execlp() do?', '`os.execlp()`: Execute the executable file (which is searched for along $PATH) with argument list args, replacing the current process.'),
    ('What does os.execlpe() do?', '`os.execlpe()`: Execute the executable file (which is searched for along $PATH) with argument list args and environment env, replacing the current process.'),
    ('What does os.execvp() do?', '`os.execvp()`: Execute the executable file (which is searched for along $PATH) with argument list args, replacing the current process. args may be a list or tuple of strings.'),
    ('What does os.execvpe() do?', '`os.execvpe()`: Execute the executable file (which is searched for along $PATH) with argument list args and environment env, replacing the current process. args may be a list or tuple of strings.'),
    ('What does os.fsdecode() do?', "`os.fsdecode()`: Decode filename (an os.PathLike, bytes, or str) from the filesystem encoding with 'surrogateescape' error handler, return str unchanged. On Windows, use 'strict' error handler if the file system encoding is 'mbcs' (which is the default encoding)."),
    ('What does os.fsencode() do?', "`os.fsencode()`: Encode filename (an os.PathLike, bytes, or str) to the filesystem encoding with 'surrogateescape' error handler, return bytes unchanged. On Windows, use 'strict' error handler if the file system encoding is 'mbcs' (which is the default encoding)."),
    ('What does os.fwalk() do?', '`os.fwalk()`: Directory tree generator.'),
    ('What does os.get_exec_path() do?', '`os.get_exec_path()`: Returns the sequence of directories that will be searched for the named executable (similar to a shell) when launching a process.'),
    ('What does os.getenv() do?', "`os.getenv()`: Get an environment variable, return None if it doesn't exist. The optional second argument can specify an alternate default. key, default and the result are str."),
    ('What does os.getenvb() do?', "`os.getenvb()`: Get an environment variable, return None if it doesn't exist. The optional second argument can specify an alternate default. key, default and the result are bytes."),
    ('What does os.makedirs() do?', '`os.makedirs()`: Super-mkdir; create a leaf directory and all intermediate ones. Works like mkdir, except that any intermediate path segment (not just the rightmost) will be created if it does not exist. If the target directory already exists, raise an OSError if exist_ok is False. Otherwise no exception is raised. This is recursive.'),
    ('What does os.removedirs() do?', '`os.removedirs()`: Super-rmdir; remove a leaf directory and all empty intermediate ones.'),
    ('What does os.renames() do?', '`os.renames()`: Super-rename; create directories as necessary and delete any left empty.'),
    ('What does os.spawnl() do?', "`os.spawnl()`: Execute file with arguments from args in a subprocess. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnle() do?', "`os.spawnle()`: Execute file with arguments from args in a subprocess with the supplied environment. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnlp() do?', "`os.spawnlp()`: Execute file (which is looked for along $PATH) with arguments from args in a subprocess with the supplied environment. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnlpe() do?', "`os.spawnlpe()`: Execute file (which is looked for along $PATH) with arguments from args in a subprocess with the supplied environment. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnv() do?', "`os.spawnv()`: Execute file with arguments from args in a subprocess. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnve() do?', "`os.spawnve()`: Execute file with arguments from args in a subprocess with the specified environment. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnvp() do?', "`os.spawnvp()`: Execute file (which is looked for along $PATH) with arguments from args in a subprocess. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.spawnvpe() do?', "`os.spawnvpe()`: Execute file (which is looked for along $PATH) with arguments from args in a subprocess with the supplied environment. If mode == P_NOWAIT return the pid of the process. If mode == P_WAIT return the process's exit code if it exits normally; otherwise return -SIG, where SIG is the signal that killed it."),
    ('What does os.stat_result() do?', '`os.stat_result()`: stat_result: Result from stat, fstat, or lstat.'),
    ('What does os.statvfs_result() do?', '`os.statvfs_result()`: statvfs_result: Result from statvfs or fstatvfs.'),
    ('What does os.terminal_size() do?', '`os.terminal_size()`: A tuple of (columns, lines) for holding terminal window size'),
    ('What does os.walk() do?', '`os.walk()`: Directory tree generator.'),
    ('What does pdb.Restart() do?', '`pdb.Restart()`: Causes a debugger to be restarted for the debugged python program.'),
    ('What does pdb.attach() do?', '`pdb.attach()`: Attach to a running process with the given PID.'),
    ('What does pdb.exit_with_permission_help_text() do?', '`pdb.exit_with_permission_help_text()`: Prints a message pointing to platform-specific permission help text and exits the program. This function is called when a PermissionError is encountered while trying to attach to a process.'),
    ('What does pdb.find_first_executable_line() do?', '`pdb.find_first_executable_line()`: Try to find the first executable line of the code object.'),
    ('What does pdb.get_default_backend() do?', '`pdb.get_default_backend()`: Get the default backend to use for Pdb instances.'),
    ('What does pdb.pm() do?', '`pdb.pm()`: Enter post-mortem debugging of the traceback found in sys.last_exc.'),
    ('What does pdb.post_mortem() do?', '`pdb.post_mortem()`: Enter post-mortem debugging of the given *traceback*, or *exception* object.'),
    ('What does pdb.run() do?', '`pdb.run()`: Execute the *statement* (given as a string or a code object) under debugger control.'),
    ('What does pdb.runcall() do?', '`pdb.runcall()`: Call the function (a function or method object, not a string) with the given arguments.'),
    ('What does pdb.runeval() do?', '`pdb.runeval()`: Evaluate the *expression* (given as a string or a code object) under debugger control.'),
    ('What does pdb.set_default_backend() do?', '`pdb.set_default_backend()`: Set the default backend to use for Pdb instances.'),
    ('What does pdb.set_trace() do?', '`pdb.set_trace()`: Enter the debugger at the calling stack frame.'),
    ('What does pdb.set_trace_async() do?', '`pdb.set_trace_async()`: Enter the debugger at the calling stack frame, but in async mode.'),
    ('What does pickle.PickleBuffer() do?', '`pickle.PickleBuffer()`: Wrapper for potentially out-of-band buffers'),
    ('What does pickle.decode_long() do?', "`pickle.decode_long()`: Decode a long from a two's complement little-endian binary string."),
    ('What does pickle.encode_long() do?', "`pickle.encode_long()`: Encode a long to a two's complement little-endian binary string. Note that 0 is a special case, returning an empty string, to save a byte in the LONG1 pickling context."),
    ('What does pickle.whichmodule() do?', '`pickle.whichmodule()`: Find the module an object belong to.'),
    ('What does pickletools.dis() do?', '`pickletools.dis()`: Produce a symbolic disassembly of a pickle.'),
    ('What does pickletools.genops() do?', '`pickletools.genops()`: Generate all the opcodes in a pickle.'),
    ('What does pickletools.optimize() do?', '`pickletools.optimize()`: Optimize a pickle string by removing unused PUT opcodes'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_bytearray8() do?', '`pickletools.read_bytearray8()`: >>> import io, struct, sys >>> read_bytearray8(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abc")) bytearray(b\'\') >>> read_bytearray8(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abcdef")) bytearray(b\'abc\') >>> bigsize8 = struct.pack("<Q", sys.maxsize//3) >>> read_bytearray8(io.BytesIO(bigsize8 + b"abcdef")) #doctest: +ELLIPSIS Traceback (most recent call last): ...'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_bytes1() do?', '`pickletools.read_bytes1()`: >>> import io >>> read_bytes1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00")) b\'\' >>> read_bytes1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03abcdef")) b\'abc\''),
    ('What does pickletools.read_bytes4() do?', '`pickletools.read_bytes4()`: >>> import io >>> read_bytes4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abc")) b\'\' >>> read_bytes4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03\\x00\\x00\\x00abcdef")) b\'abc\' >>> read_bytes4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x03abcdef")) Traceback (most recent call last): ... ValueError: expected 50331648 bytes in a bytes4, but only 6 remain'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_bytes8() do?', '`pickletools.read_bytes8()`: >>> import io, struct, sys >>> read_bytes8(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abc")) b\'\' >>> read_bytes8(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abcdef")) b\'abc\' >>> bigsize8 = struct.pack("<Q", sys.maxsize//3) >>> read_bytes8(io.BytesIO(bigsize8 + b"abcdef")) #doctest: +ELLIPSIS Traceback (most recent call last): ...'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_decimalnl_long() do?', '`pickletools.read_decimalnl_long()`: >>> import io'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_decimalnl_short() do?', '`pickletools.read_decimalnl_short()`: >>> import io >>> read_decimalnl_short(io.BytesIO(b"1234\\n56")) 1234'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_float8() do?', '`pickletools.read_float8()`: >>> import io, struct >>> raw = struct.pack(">d", -1.25) >>> raw b\'\\xbf\\xf4\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\' >>> read_float8(io.BytesIO(raw + b"\\n")) -1.25'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_floatnl() do?', '`pickletools.read_floatnl()`: >>> import io >>> read_floatnl(io.BytesIO(b"-1.25\\n6")) -1.25'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_int4() do?', "`pickletools.read_int4()`: >>> import io >>> read_int4(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff\\x00\\x00\\x00')) 255 >>> read_int4(io.BytesIO(b'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x80')) == -(2**31) True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_long1() do?', '`pickletools.read_long1()`: >>> import io >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00")) 0 >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\xff\\x00")) 255 >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\xff\\x7f")) 32767 >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\xff")) -256 >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\x80")) -32768'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_long4() do?', '`pickletools.read_long4()`: >>> import io >>> read_long4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\xff\\x00")) 255 >>> read_long4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\xff\\x7f")) 32767 >>> read_long4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\xff")) -256 >>> read_long4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x80")) -32768 >>> read_long1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00")) 0'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_string1() do?', '`pickletools.read_string1()`: >>> import io >>> read_string1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00")) \'\' >>> read_string1(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03abcdef")) \'abc\''),
    ('What does pickletools.read_string4() do?', '`pickletools.read_string4()`: >>> import io >>> read_string4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00abc")) \'\' >>> read_string4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x03\\x00\\x00\\x00abcdef")) \'abc\' >>> read_string4(io.BytesIO(b"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x03abcdef")) Traceback (most recent call last): ... ValueError: expected 50331648 bytes in a string4, but only 6 remain'),
    ('What does pickletools.read_stringnl() do?', '`pickletools.read_stringnl()`: >>> import io >>> read_stringnl(io.BytesIO(b"\'abcd\'\\nefg\\n")) \'abcd\''),
    ('What does pickletools.read_stringnl_noescape_pair() do?', '`pickletools.read_stringnl_noescape_pair()`: >>> import io >>> read_stringnl_noescape_pair(io.BytesIO(b"Queue\\nEmpty\\njunk")) \'Queue Empty\''),
    ('What does pickletools.read_uint1() do?', "`pickletools.read_uint1()`: >>> import io >>> read_uint1(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff')) 255"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_uint2() do?', "`pickletools.read_uint2()`: >>> import io >>> read_uint2(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff\\x00')) 255 >>> read_uint2(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff\\xff')) 65535"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_uint4() do?', "`pickletools.read_uint4()`: >>> import io >>> read_uint4(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff\\x00\\x00\\x00')) 255 >>> read_uint4(io.BytesIO(b'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x80')) == 2**31 True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_uint8() do?', "`pickletools.read_uint8()`: >>> import io >>> read_uint8(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00')) 255 >>> read_uint8(io.BytesIO(b'\\xff' * 8)) == 2**64-1 True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_unicodestring1() do?', "`pickletools.read_unicodestring1()`: >>> import io >>> s = 'abcd\\uabcd' >>> enc = s.encode('utf-8') >>> enc b'abcd\\xea\\xaf\\x8d' >>> n = bytes([len(enc)]) # little-endian 1-byte length >>> t = read_unicodestring1(io.BytesIO(n + enc + b'junk')) >>> s == t True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_unicodestring4() do?', "`pickletools.read_unicodestring4()`: >>> import io >>> s = 'abcd\\uabcd' >>> enc = s.encode('utf-8') >>> enc b'abcd\\xea\\xaf\\x8d' >>> n = bytes([len(enc), 0, 0, 0]) # little-endian 4-byte length >>> t = read_unicodestring4(io.BytesIO(n + enc + b'junk')) >>> s == t True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_unicodestring8() do?', "`pickletools.read_unicodestring8()`: >>> import io >>> s = 'abcd\\uabcd' >>> enc = s.encode('utf-8') >>> enc b'abcd\\xea\\xaf\\x8d' >>> n = bytes([len(enc)]) + b'\\0' * 7 # little-endian 8-byte length >>> t = read_unicodestring8(io.BytesIO(n + enc + b'junk')) >>> s == t True"),
    ('What does pickletools.read_unicodestringnl() do?', '`pickletools.read_unicodestringnl()`: >>> import io >>> read_unicodestringnl(io.BytesIO(b"abc\\\\uabcd\\njunk")) == \'abc\\uabcd\' True'),
    ('What does pkgutil.ModuleInfo() do?', '`pkgutil.ModuleInfo()`: A namedtuple with minimal info about a module.'),
    ('What does pkgutil.extend_path() do?', "`pkgutil.extend_path()`: Extend a package's path."),
    ('What does pkgutil.get_data() do?', '`pkgutil.get_data()`: Get a resource from a package.'),
    ('What does pkgutil.get_importer() do?', '`pkgutil.get_importer()`: Retrieve a finder for the given path item'),
    ('What does pkgutil.iter_importers() do?', '`pkgutil.iter_importers()`: Yield finders for the given module name'),
    ('What does pkgutil.iter_modules() do?', '`pkgutil.iter_modules()`: Yields ModuleInfo for all submodules on path, or, if path is None, all top-level modules on sys.path.'),
    ('What does pkgutil.resolve_name() do?', '`pkgutil.resolve_name()`: Resolve a name to an object.'),
    ('What does pkgutil.walk_packages() do?', '`pkgutil.walk_packages()`: Yields ModuleInfo for all modules recursively on path, or, if path is None, all accessible modules.'),
    ('What does platform.architecture() do?', '`platform.architecture()`: Queries the given executable (defaults to the Python interpreter binary) for various architecture information.'),
    ('What does platform.freedesktop_os_release() do?', '`platform.freedesktop_os_release()`: Return operation system identification from freedesktop.org os-release'),
    ('What does platform.invalidate_caches() do?', '`platform.invalidate_caches()`: Invalidate the cached results.'),
    ('What does platform.ios_ver() do?', '`platform.ios_ver()`: Get iOS version information, and return it as a namedtuple: (system, release, model, is_simulator).'),
    ('What does platform.java_ver() do?', '`platform.java_ver()`: Version interface for Jython.'),
    ('What does platform.libc_ver() do?', '`platform.libc_ver()`: Tries to determine the libc version that the file executable (which defaults to the Python interpreter) is linked against.'),
    ('What does platform.mac_ver() do?', '`platform.mac_ver()`: Get macOS version information and return it as tuple (release, versioninfo, machine) with versioninfo being a tuple (version, dev_stage, non_release_version).'),
    ('What does platform.machine() do?', "`platform.machine()`: Returns the machine type, e.g. 'i386'"),
    ('What does platform.node() do?', "`platform.node()`: Returns the computer's network name (which may not be fully qualified)"),
    ('What does platform.platform() do?', '`platform.platform()`: Returns a single string identifying the underlying platform with as much useful information as possible (but no more :).'),
    ('What does platform.processor() do?', "`platform.processor()`: Returns the (true) processor name, e.g. 'amdk6'"),
