    ('What does unittest.mock.MagicMock() do?', '`unittest.mock.MagicMock()`: MagicMock is a subclass of Mock with default implementations of most of the magic methods. You can use MagicMock without having to configure the magic methods yourself.'),
    ('What does unittest.mock.Mock() do?', '`unittest.mock.Mock()`: Create a new `Mock` object. `Mock` takes several optional arguments that specify the behaviour of the Mock object:'),
