    ('What does urllib.parse.urljoin() do?', '`urllib.parse.urljoin()`: Join a base URL and a possibly relative URL to form an absolute interpretation of the latter.'),
    ('What does urllib.parse.urlparse() do?', '`urllib.parse.urlparse()`: Parse a URL into 6 components: <scheme>://<netloc>/<path>;<params>?<query>#<fragment>'),
    ('What does urllib.parse.urlsplit() do?', '`urllib.parse.urlsplit()`: Parse a URL into 5 components: <scheme>://<netloc>/<path>?<query>#<fragment>'),
    ('What does urllib.parse.urlunparse() do?', '`urllib.parse.urlunparse()`: Put a parsed URL back together again. This may result in a slightly different, but equivalent URL, if the URL that was parsed originally had redundant delimiters, e.g. a ? with an empty query (the draft states that these are equivalent).'),
